            <div xml:id="d405-a2">

                <pb facs="0520" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg408"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Northcott to the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-05-12"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 41.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your excellency’s esteemed note of December 20, 1909, which your
                    excellency was good enough to hand to me personally yesterday. In reply I beg to
                    say that I have noted your excellency’s sentiments in regard to the treaties of
                    Washington, and that I will duly transmit them to my Government.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elliott
                    Northcott.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
